# `ScopeBoundary`

<SymbolMeta />
<SymbolSignature />

`ScopeBoundary` joins one `StaticScope` to its sole valid [`ScopeParent`](./ScopeParent). Construct it as a static value with `ScopeBoundary::new(&ScopeType, parent)` and place it in the protocol's [`ScopeTopology`](./ScopeTopology).

The boundary captures stable scope identity, diagnostic name, and rank from `StaticScope`. The parent relation is structural rather than advisory: a runtime cannot correctly open the boundary under another parent, and the application rejects topology declarations whose parent cannot outlive the child.

Use one boundary per openable protocol scope. Do not use boundaries to restate the framework-owned root scope; select `ScopeParent::Root` for a protocol scope whose immediate parent is the application root.

